{"body":{"says":"One word where it was said, a proposal beside the drafted Term, which is to be settled with it: its place is its locality, the sentence, paragraph and utterance holding it. What it shares with the same word elsewhere is its lexeme, which it only points at."},"id":"1M6YBY3G0000005","instance":[],"mould":{"after":{"optional":true,"says":"Marks standing after the word, as a comma or full stop.","shape":"string"},"before":{"optional":true,"says":"Marks standing before the word, as an opening quote or bracket.","shape":"string"},"text":{"says":"The word meant, without the marks around it; a run of marks alone is a word of its own.","shape":"string"},"typed":{"optional":true,"says":"The word as typed or heard, where it differs from what was meant.","shape":"string"}},"name":"word"}